diff --git a/docs/routing.rst b/docs/routing.rst
index 5df9e974..1b2c2be3 100644
--- a/docs/routing.rst
+++ b/docs/routing.rst
@@ -101,6 +101,17 @@ mode. Variable parts are not equal if they use different converters, although
 this heuristic may not be perfect depending on what the different converters can
 actually match.
 
+Equal rules are only duplicates if they share a method, since the earlier rule
+would always be matched for that method. A rule without ``methods`` matches any
+method. ``HEAD`` and ``OPTIONS`` are often added automatically (``HEAD`` is
+added if ``GET`` is present), so sharing only those is allowed unless the new
+rule has no other methods left to match.
+
+``strict_slashes`` does not affect duplicates. A rule with a trailing slash is
+not equal to the same rule without one, and each is still matched by its own
+URL. ``merge_slashes`` is applied to the rule before comparing, so with it
+enabled ``/a//b`` duplicates ``/a/b``.
+
 
 Rule Priority
 =============
